   150	   * bare `\r` is ordinary content, because only `\n` terminates.
   151	   *
   152	   * A trailing terminator does **not** produce a phantom empty final line, so
   153	   * a well-formed journal yields exactly as many slices as it has entries.
   154	   * Interior blank lines *are* returned — they are real bytes at real offsets,
   155	   * and hiding them would make the offsets lie.
